  "body": "The maintainer reported this in chat on 2026-11-22, in his own words:\n\n> Bug; the \"do not touch\" feature under boundaries, should allow me to pick a face or an edge. But i does not..\n\nHe did not say which operation kind he used, or what happens on a click. The worker finds this first.\n\n## What the code says\n\nThe feature is #2055 (closed). The wanted behaviour: the \"Do not touch\" group of the Geometry tab lets the user click faces and edges in the viewport. Each pick shows as a row with a remove button.\n\nTwo readings of the report. The worker checks both:\n\n1. The group is not usable for the operation kind that the maintainer uses. `do_not_touch_unsupported` (`crates/app/src/operation/types/avoid.rs:54`) says: \"'Do not touch' is supported on 2D Offset and 3D Pocket operations only so far\". For each other kind the group shows only that sentence. There is no \"Pick protected\" button (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/boundary.rs:305-314`). The wording \"clear it on {kind}\" does not say how to pick, and the group still shows in the Boundaries area where the user expects a pick control.\n2. The group is usable (2D Offset, 3D Pocket), but the viewport click does not fill it. The click path is `take_pick` -> `take_do_not_touch_pick` (`crates/ui/src/boundary_draft.rs:355-398`). A click may go to the selection and not to the group, for example when a vertex is hit (the code ignores vertices), or when the group is in the \"Picking…\" state but another pick tool holds the viewport.\n\n## Expected\n\n- For each operation kind that has the group, a click on a face or an edge adds a row to \"Do not touch\". The status line says what was added.\n- For a kind that does not support it, the user sees why, in plain words, and what to do. The better answer is to support the kind (the maintainer asked for \"do not touch\" on operations in #2055: \"the calculation should avoid to gouge them at all costs\").\n\n## Done means\n\n- A structural test in `crates/ui`: with the group open, a face click and an edge click each add one row; a remove click takes it away; the status line names the pick.\n- The worker names the operation kind and the exact reason in a comment on this issue. If the cause is reading 1, the worker files one sub-issue per kind that lacks the feature (`Refs #2055`, bug, P3, source:agent, effort by the table; the safety floor applies to the generator work).\n- The change goes through the same undoable command and MCP tool as the existing \"Do not touch\" picks.\n",
